      "name": "Ahupuaʻa",
      "description": "Land divisions running ridge to reef. Each holds a full slice of the rainfall gradient — wet uplands, a stream, dry coast — so a community had everything it needed within one boundary. The lines follow the terrain because the terrain is what they were drawn from.",
